<h1>Measure_Circle</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> Calls a wizard for capture/scan datum circle using the localiser probe/sensor.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Parameters</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>Name</b></i></span>  name of the resulting datum circle that will be created.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>Prompt</b></i></span>  text to be used on the first step of the wizard: Available values are:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Empty string ( <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>""</i></span> )  wizard should display the default text.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Non-empty string  wizard should use this string.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>Method</b></i></span>  determines measurement method. Available values are:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Capture</i></span>  uses probe to measure the datum circle.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Scan</i></span>  uses scanning to measure the datum circle. When this value is used the following parameters are ignored: <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>BasePlane</i></span>, <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Compensation</i></span>, and <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>MaxPoints</i></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>BasePlane</b></i></span>  determines what plane to be used for projecting the datum circle. Available values are:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Empty string ( <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>""</i></span> )  plane should be captured.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Non-empty string  name of the plane / plane-reducible entity that should be used for projection.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>Compensation</b></i></span>  determines compensation. Available values are:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Capture</i></span>  lets user to capture point for compensation.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Internal</i></span>  automatically inflates the circle's radius with the probe radius.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>External</i></span>  automatically deflates the circle's radius with the probe radius.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>ImmediateAccept</b></i></span>  determines the behaviour of the wizard when finish. Available values are:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Yes</i></span>  when finish capture the datum circle will be created silently, i.e. no Accept/Reject dialog.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>No</i></span>  when finish capture Accept/Reject dialog with the results should be displayed and user could select whether to accept or reject the circle.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>MaxPoints</b></i></span>  limits number of the points that should be captured for the circle. If it is zero number of points is unlimited, i.e. default behaviour of the wizard. If it is higher than zero then when last point is captured wizard finishes automatically, i.e. without pressing Finish button. Accept/Reject dialog appears optionally  depending on the value of <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>ImmediateAccept</i></span> parameter. Minimum number of points for circle is 3.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>PlaneIndex</b></i></span>  specifies the base plane (first if <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>1</i></span> and second if <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>2</i></span>) when cylinder entity is used for <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>BasePlane</i></span> parameter. In all other cases this parameter is ignored. Default value is 0.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>UI Commands</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span><i style="font-style:italic;">Datum &gt; Circle</i></span> from the localiser driven menu<span style="font-style:italic;"><i>.</i></span></p>
<p class="Warning">'Base plane definition' option from <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Datum Capture</i></span> dialog does not apply when the circle is captured via macro command. 'Out of tolerance' &#160;and 'Sheet metal measurement' options from <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Datum Capture</i></span> dialog apply (if enabled) when the circle is captured via macro command. Continue capturing (Yes/No) dialog is not displayed. Wizard is terminated when finish capture and optionally accept/reject entity.</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Example:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Measure_Circle( Name="Circle 1", Prompt="Capture Circle 1", Method="Capture", BasePlane="", Compensation="Capture", ImmediateAccept=Yes, MaxPoints=0, PlaneIndex=0 )</p>
